  "details": "<div>Nersae, referred to by Vergil, was a <em>vicus </em>of the Aequiculi that likely constituted the <em>res publica Aequiculanorum</em> in the <em>tribus Fabia</em>.</div>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Referred to by Virgil, Nersa was a vicus of the Aequiculi. Its precise location is not known, but some 19th century scholars identified it with the modern village of Civitella di Nesce in Italy.",
